CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold as a demonstrated realistic workload result. Evidence is CPU-only constructed traces, 400 turns/cell, no real agent traces, no GPU serving system, no real KV-cache/preemption costs, and no measured production abandonment distribution. At L0, deprioritize-only reclaims 0 slots and kill-on-flag reclaims only 0.4-3.4% total decode while destroying 2.2-18.6% completed turns.
RATIONALE: The core systems claim fails on its own evidence: the only non-kill scheduler action, deprioritization, reclaims zero compute and worsens completed-turn p99 by +18% to +317%; the only reclaiming action is generic request kill/preemption and has unacceptable false-positive harm at AUC ~0.71. Existing systems already ship the underlying mechanisms: vLLM documents preemption/recompute for KV pressure and supports priority scheduling; SGLang exposes priority scheduling/preemption and abort paths; TensorRT-LLM exposes pluggable schedulers; Llumnix and FastServe cover runtime rescheduling/preemptive scheduling as named prior work. The agent-abandonment signal could have been the systems insight, but the packet only shows a constructed-trace conditional predictor and no real trace oracle ceiling, so there is insufficient evidence that it transfers beyond glue over existing schedulers.
